    "result_text": "All 9 test classes (17 tests) pass, including the new `Cp09Tests`. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for new owners in this Spring Boot PetClinic REST app. The code is `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the last name, a hyphen, and a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count (e.g. `SMI-0007`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to the `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table (tests run on the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema file is the source of truth; I updated all four for consistency).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct auto-maps it onto the GET response.\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, compute and set the code before saving via a new `nextCustomerCode(...)` helper. The sequence is `findAllOwners().size() + 1` evaluated *before* the new owner is persisted, so consecutive creates increment by one as required.\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint (V1, `/api`) is what the acceptance tests hit \u2014 V2 lives under `/v2/owners` and is untouched. `Cp09Tests` verifies the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that the two owners' sequence numbers differ by exactly one; all pre-existing tests remain green.",
